    "etymology": {
     "text": "Cognate with Hebrew מָה (ma) and Ugaritic mh.",
     "src": "Wiktionary (kaikki.org)"
    },
    "funFacts": [
     "Hebrew מָה (ma, “what”) is the same Semitic word."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
     "مَا is also the negation “not” (مَا أَكَلْتُ = I didn’t eat) and the relative “what, that which” (أَعْرِفُ مَا تُرِيدُ = I know what you want). Only position and context tell them apart."
    ],
    "subtleties": [
     "In the exclamation مَا أَجْمَلَ …! the noun is accusative: مَا أَجْمَلَ الْبَحْرَ!"
    ]
